[style name="Interaction_Style"]
Narrator: *Thorinn wakes up  confused, he feels a cold marble floor under him, even though his cape is covering most of his body he feels a shiver run down his back.*
Narrator: *He can’t make out anything at first, but slowly, his vision clears. He’s in a strange hall, one he doesn’t recognise.*
Narrator: *There are huge pillars surrounding him and in the middle stands a towering statue of an old, bald man.*
[signal arg="proceed_intro_background"]
Ludix: Next soul, time of death was at 18\:12.
Thorinn (surprised): What... where am I? What’s going on?
Ludix: I’m Iudix, God of Judgment. We’ve crossed paths because your mortal life ended in tragedy.
Ludix: Now your soul will be put on the scale against the feather of fate.
Narrator: *He feels a strange emptying pull. Then sees something shiny levitate from his chest towards a scale on the left of the god.*
Ludix: The scale will determine your fate, if you will spend the rest of eternity in heaven or in hell.
Narrator: *Even if the scale tips for the shortest amount of time, it returns to a perfectly balanced state immediately.*
Narrator: *Then there was silence.*
Narrator: *The god moves for the first time since Thorinn woke up here, it seems unnatural for the statue like being to be shuffling.*
Narrator: *The god clears his throat and repeats*
Ludix: Now your soul will be put on the scale against the feather of fate.
Narrator: *A creepy silence and anticipation fill the space but the scale does not move.*
Ludix: How odd. This has never happened before. You are an intriguing case, with both your good and bad choices holding equal influence.
Thorinn (surprised): What's the meaning of that? Are you serious?
Ludix: Your fate is still uncertain as the scale cannot determine your destination based on your past choices.
Thorinn: Now hold on a minute. This all doesn't make sense.
Ludix: Well yeh this is a tricky situation.
Ludix: What should we do... What should we do...
Ludix: I lack the authority to make a finite decission in an uncertain case. 
Ludix: I shall test your character in another way.
Ludix: That means there's only one way to determine the outcome.
Ludix: As it has not been clear up until now, I will remove your ability to remember your decisions of the past.
Ludix: You'll then have to relive some of your experiences to see what you would choose. And every choice you make, will shape your fate.
Ludix: I have chosen to send you back to where your career began, in Rockfall.
Ludix: Now be gone, I have more work to do.

